{
  "id": "can-013",
  "description": "Raw-JSON hashing of canonical whole-second timestamps. RFC-ACDP-0001 §5.3/§5.7 already require hashing the body as received; this vector closes a coverage gap: no earlier vector pins a CANONICAL millisecond timestamp whose fraction is .000. A verifier that recomputes content_hash from a typed round-trip (e.g. a date-time type whose default serializer drops a zero fraction, re-emitting 2026-12-31T23:59:59.000Z as 2026-12-31T23:59:59Z) reports a false hash_mismatch on a conformant body. Registries and consumers MUST reproduce the first vector's hash. Deployment note: a registry build with that defect rejects bodies from producers that emit the canonical .000Z form; upgrade registries before producers.",
  "tags": [
    "canonicalization",
    "hashing",
    "timestamps"
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "Canonical .000 fractions — conformant",
      "input": {
